-- title:
--   Boundedness of aₚ from agreement with the lift-trace seed
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $e$ be a group isomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$; let $H$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ and write $\mathrm{fixFld}\ H$ for the intermediate field of $H$-fixed points of $L$. Let $\Phi$ be a Hecke eigensystem over $\mathbb{Q}$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, that is, a nonzero level ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with functions $p \mapsto \Phi.a\,p$ and $p \mapsto \Phi.b\,p$ on the height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Form `formalBaseChange` of $\Phi$ to $\mathrm{fixFld}\ H$: it has level $\top$, and at a height-one prime $\mathfrak{P}$ lying under $p$ with $f = \mathrm{inertiaDeg}'(p,\mathfrak{P})$ its entries are $\mathrm{satakePow}\ f\ (\Phi.a\,p)\ (\Phi.b\,p)$ and $(\Phi.b\,p)^f$, where $\mathrm{satakePow}$ is given by the recursion with values $2$, $s$ and $s\cdot\mathrm{satakePow}\,(n+1) - e\cdot\mathrm{satakePow}\,n$. Form also `liftTraceSeed e H`, the eigensystem over $\mathrm{fixFld}\ H$ with values in $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ of level $\top$ whose entries at $w$ are the trace and determinant of $\mathrm{liftOf}(e(\mathrm{seedFrob}\ H\ w))$, a chosen matrix in the monoid generated by $S_{\mathrm{lift}}, T_{\mathrm{lift}}$ reducing mod $3$ to the given element, and push it into $\mathbb{C}$ by the ring homomorphism sending $\sqrt{-2}$ to $\sqrt{2}\,i$. Assume these two eigensystems over $\mathrm{fixFld}\ H$ agree, in both entries, at all height-one primes outside some finite set. Then there is a real $C$ with $\|\Phi.a\,p\| \le C$ for every height-one prime $p$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This supplies the archimedean boundedness of the rational eigensystem's trace entries which, in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the argument, accompanies the identification of a complex eigensystem with the lift of a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$-valued Galois datum. It is used in the construction of the agreeing cuspidal pair attached to such a lift.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_exists_forall_norm_a_le_of_formalBaseChange_agrees_liftTraceSeed.lean

